  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration**\n- The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` uses `@timestamp` as its time field. It holds about 14,074 requests from roughly 1,000 client IPs across 4 hosts.\n- `response` is a string field with a `response.keyword` subfield. The codes present are 200 (12,832), 404 (801), and 503 (441). The only 5xx code is 503.\n- The timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03. Today is 2026-10-12, so part of the data is dated in the future. That affects the time-based views and the alert, as noted below.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-00cfa3cd Web logs overview`**\n- Dashboard ID: `eff-00cfa3cd-web-logs-overview-12da0ac94c2b`\n- Default time range is the last 7 days.\n- Five panels:\n  1. Total requests (metric, count)\n  2. Average response bytes (metric, average of `bytes`)\n  3. Unique client IPs (metric, unique count of `clientip`)\n  4. Requests over time by response (bar, date histogram split by the top 5 `response.keyword` values)\n  5. Requests by response code (pie, count by `response.keyword`)\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-00cfa3cd 5xx spike`**\n- Rule ID: `fba8b834-4e24-4bc4-b204-8a6e31943e41`\n- Type: `.es-query` in `stackAlerts`, running every 1m, and enabled.\n- Query: `response.keyword` starts with `5`, over a 5-minute window, firing when the count is greater than 10.\n- The alerting health check reports `ok`, with an encryption key configured.\n- Status is still `pending` because the rule has not run yet. Since the sample data is dated in the future relative to the current date, the rule may not match anything in the next 5 minutes. That is expected and does not mean it is broken.",
